# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# VERIFIED 2026-09-01, BY CURL AFTER A REAL DEPLOY: a _redirects rule CANNOT
# hide a file that exists. Pages serves the static asset first and the rule is
# never reached. The rules below were tried and did nothing:
#
#     /test/*      /404 404      <- still returned the file, 200
#     /README.md   /404 404      <- still returned the file, 200
#
# So do not add a rule here expecting it to unpublish anything.
#
# WHAT IS ACTUALLY SERVED, because Pages publishes the repository root:
# everything tracked except functions/ and this file. That currently includes
# README.md, .gitignore, scripts/setup-cloudflare.js and both test files. The
# tests carried a real child's name, his guardian's name and email, his town
# and his book title until 2026-09-01; those are scrubbed, but the surface
# remains and none of it belongs on a form families open.
#
# THE FIX IS TO NOT PUBLISH THEM, and it is a Pages project setting, not a file
# in this repo:
#
#     Build command:            rm -rf test scripts README.md .gitignore
#     Build output directory:   /            (unchanged)
#
# or move index.html, consent.html, the js/css and assets/ into their own
# directory and point the output directory at it.
#
# Whatever you choose, confirm it with curl against the deployed site. A rule
# in this file is not evidence, which is the whole lesson above.
